# === The composition graph ===
#
# The autopoietic Rust→mirror translation composition expression
# (Alex 2026-07-16 verbatim, session-crystallizing):
#
#   @fate.roll(
#     @glue(@code/rust, @shatter),      ← fragmentation lens
#     @kintsugi/algebra                   ← candidate pool
#                                            (speaker-pair metalogue-
#                                             session; 15 landed
#                                             elements + future turns)
#   ) → winning fracture                   ← one turn in the session
#     → @glue(_, @mirror)                    ← translation morphism
#     → @bauchladen.crystallize             ← write-back to tray
#     → grows @silicon/algebra              ← memory speaker gains turn
#     → grows @fate/algebra                 ← structure speaker gains turn
#
# Substrate primitives composed (ALL REFERENCED; NONE REDECLARED):
#
#   Primitive                                Path                                                     Role
#   --------------------------------------   ------------------------------------------------------   ------------------------------------------------
#   @code/rust                               shards/code/rust.mirror                                  source-side altitude (a `.rs` path ref)
#   @shatter                                 shards/shatter.mirror (family-root)                      fragmentation prism composed via @glue
#   @glue                                    shards/glue.mirror                                       morphism-category family-root; @glue(A, B)
#                                                                                                     is a correspondence carrier per
#                                                                                                     `type correspondence` at :561-566
#   @glue.propose(source, target)            shards/glue.mirror :621                                  enumerate admissible correspondences
#   @glue.translate(c, payload)              shards/glue.mirror :662                                  apply the morphism via @fate
#   @fate.roll(algebra, hole)                shards/fate.mirror                                       dice-roll over restricted state space
#   @kintsugi/algebra                        shards/kintsugi.mirror :237-241 + :263-267               candidate pool (typed record binding
#                                                                                                     via `kintsugi_algebra` + bilateral
#                                                                                                     `kintsugi_algebra_witnessing`);
#                                                                                                     15 landed fracture species + future turns
#   @mirror                                  shards/mirror.mirror                                     target-side altitude (a mirror shard-path)
#   @bauchladen.crystallize(record)          shards/bauchladen.mirror                                 write-back extending both speaker-algebras
#   @io/fs.read(path)                        shards/io/fs.mirror                                      byte-read of the source .rs file
#   @io/git.commit(msg, author, allow_empty) shards/io/git.mirror                                     mirror-authored commit per
#                                                                                                     bilateral_arm_redundant precedent
#                                                                                                     (author = "mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>")
#
# === Composition-graph enumeration (docblock; the action body is
#     `\`-obligation-blocked per craft-not-deliver) ===
#
# The `translate_rust_to_mirror(source, target_shard_path)` action
# below composes the following edges. Each edge is a reference; no
# primitive is redeclared. The action body is `\`-blocked; Reed
# follow-up ticks realise the edges through `apply_h::act` composition
# after `@fate.roll` + `@glue.compose` resolvers land.
#
#   Edge 1 (READ):
#     `@io/fs.read(source)` → rust_bytes
#     Reads the source .rs file as bytes. `source` is a ref whose
#     altitude namespace is `@code/rust` (a .rs path per
#     `shards/code/rust.mirror`); the read is at `@io/fs` altitude
#     per the boundary discipline.
#
#   Edge 2 (FRAGMENT via @glue):
#     `@glue.propose(@code/rust, @shatter)` → [correspondence]
#     → rust_fragments = @glue.translate(correspondence, rust_bytes)
#     Alex's compositional decl `@glue(@code/rust, @shatter)` names
#     the fragmentation lens: a Mesland-category correspondence from
#     the source altitude (@code/rust) to the shatter altitude
#     (@shatter). The correspondence's restriction bounds the
#     admissible morphisms; @fate selects one within the restriction
#     per `@glue.translate` at `shards/glue.mirror :662`.
#
#   Edge 3 (ROLL over @kintsugi/algebra):
#     `@fate.roll(hole = rust_fragments, algebra = @kintsugi/algebra)`
#     → dice_roll
#     The tournament over the candidate pool: `@fate/algebra` speaker
#     proposes structural candidates (per `shards/fate.mirror`
#     §"literal roll of the dice"); `@silicon/algebra` speaker
#     realises those with crystallized past-translations (per
#     `shards/silicon/algebra.mirror` §"what crystallizes here"). The
#     `@kintsugi/algebra` binding at `shards/kintsugi.mirror` :237-241
#     is the intersection surface both speakers dispatch through. The
#     roll's typed restriction is `@kintsugi/algebra`'s element-set
#     (15 landed + future).
#
#   Edge 4 (WINNING FRACTURE → turn):
#     The dice_roll names one `@kintsugi/fracture/*` species (one
#     turn in the session). The winning fracture IS the algebra-
#     element the two speakers jointly discharged Pass on.
#
#   Edge 5 (TRANSLATE via @glue):
#     `@glue.propose(winning_fracture, @mirror)` → [correspondence]
#     → mirror_bytes = @glue.translate(correspondence, rust_fragments)
#     The translation morphism from the winning fracture (a source-
#     side species) to `@mirror` (the target substrate altitude); the
#     morphism produces mirror composition bytes at the target-side
#     algebra A_@mirror.
#
#   Edge 6 (WRITE-BACK via @bauchladen):
#     `outcome = translation_outcome { correspondence, selected_
#                                       morphism, payload =
#                                       mirror_bytes, transparency }`
#     `@bauchladen.crystallize(outcome)` → pass|failure
#     The outcome lands as a crystal under `@fate/algebra/morphism`
#     path-namespace per Mara `a18ca90` precedent. The write-back
#     grows BOTH speaker-algebras: `@silicon/algebra` gains a
#     `routine` crystal (empirical memory of the translation);
#     `@fate/algebra` gains a `@fate/algebra/morphism` crystal
#     (structural possibility now populated).
#
#   Edge 7 (EMIT to target shard-path):
#     `@io/fs.write(target_shard_path, mirror_bytes)` → imperfect
#     Writes the winning composition's mirror bytes to the target
#     shard path. (Composition; Reed follow-up ticks realise the
#     write surface — the substrate has `@io/fs.mutate_at` at empty-
#     replacement altitude landed via Mara Landing 7; whole-file
#     write is `mutate_at` at file-full-replacement altitude.)
#
#   Edge 8 (COMMIT under mirror-authorship):
#     `@io/git.commit(msg, "mirror <mirror@spectral.engineer>",
#                     allow_empty=false)` → verdict
#     Per `@kintsugi/fracture/bilateral_arm_redundant` precedent
#     (`fa569ce`): the compiler authors the commit itself. `mirror
#     <mirror@spectral.engineer>`, not Reed. Reproduces the
#     `ad52973`+`20047c2` empirical shape at translation altitude.
#
#   Edge 9 (GROW both speaker-algebras — monotonic algebra extension):
#     After Edge 6's crystallization, `@kintsugi/algebra`'s element
#     count is +1 (Reading B monotonicity per canonical spec §2.2).
#     `@fate/algebra`'s path-namespace gains one
#     `@fate/algebra/morphism` crystal. `@silicon/algebra`'s tray
#     gains one `routine` crystal. The next invocation sees the
#     enlarged candidate pool (self-growing per canonical spec §5).
#
# === The fixed-point condition ===
#
# Per canonical spec §2.3 + §5: `translate_rust_to_mirror` reaches a
# fixed point when NO Rust module in `bootstrap/src/` carries
# untranslated behavior — the compiler's own
# `mirror roomba --translate=<rs-file>` walk over the bootstrap
# emits zero winning fractures because every rust-side pattern has
# a corresponding `@kintsugi/fracture/*` element AND every element's
# translation has crystallized.
#
# The paper's §14 `attending` operator at λ₀ IS this composition's
# terminal state: the fixed-point where `@kintsugi/algebra`'s
# composition-closure equals its element-closure and the substrate
# recognises itself AS an algebra (Foerster's double-closure at the
# algebra altitude; canonical spec §10.1).
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# 1. `@glue.propose` + `@glue.translate` (`shards/glue.mirror` :621
#    + :662; Mara P5 2026-06-30 + roster update 2026-07-01) — the
