  focus  translation
  project translation
  split  translation
  shift  translation
  settle translation
}

# === translation_witnessing — bilateral predicate (arity 1) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING witnessing predicate. Discharges Pass iff the
# translation outcome preserves semantics from the source (@code/rust)
# to the target (@mirror) under the winning fracture's morphism.
# The compiler's own proof that the Rust→mirror translation was
# substrate-honest.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `kintsugi_algebra_witnessing(binding)` at `shards/kintsugi.
#     mirror` :263-267 (the algebra-binding well-formedness bilateral)
#   - `arm_is_redundant_witnessing(record)` at `shards/kintsugi/
#     fracture/bilateral_arm_redundant.mirror` :494-500 (the
#     retirement-safety bilateral)
#   - `glue_witnessing(c)` at `shards/glue.mirror` :809 (the
#     morphism-category inheritance predicate; `translation_
#     witnessing` composes over `glue_witnessing` on both @glue
#     correspondences — Edge 2's fragmentation + Edge 5's translation)
#
# Discharge composition (docblock; realized via `apply_h::act` corpus
# dispatch per `a0f4d3f` reflective evaluator):
#
#   translation_witnessing(outcome) := Pass iff
#     glue_witnessing(outcome.fragmentation_correspondence) = Pass
#     ∧ glue_witnessing(outcome.translation_correspondence) = Pass
#     ∧ fate_witnessing(outcome.dice_roll) = Pass
#     ∧ kintsugi_algebra_witnessing(outcome.algebra_binding) = Pass
#     ∧ bauchladen_witnessing(outcome.crystal) = Pass
#     ∧ outcome.selected_morphism.oid ∈ @kintsugi/algebra element-set
#
# The six-conjunct composition names the substrate-honest guarantee:
# the fragmentation lens (Edge 2) is a well-typed @glue morphism; the
# translation morphism (Edge 5) is a well-typed @glue morphism; the
# @fate roll (Edge 3) is within the typed restriction; the
# @kintsugi/algebra binding is well-formed; the crystallization (Edge
# 6) landed as a well-typed crystal; and the winning fracture IS an
# element of `@kintsugi/algebra` (Reading B membership: the turn's
# body is one of the 15 landed fracture species OR a future crystallized
# element).
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: composition of six Rice-safe
# bilaterals + one set-membership check; no program-semantics
# inspection beyond byte-visible state.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `translation=discharged` — the byte-
# level substrate-decl'd marker. When all six conjuncts discharge
# Pass, the realization layer stamps the sentinel; discharge is
# byte-equality on the ref.oid containment check per
# `@epistemologic/pact/bilateral.discharge`.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]];
# Reed follow-up tick B composes this via `apply_h::act` (the
# reflective evaluator handles this bilateral through corpus
# dispatch of the six sub-witnessing predicates + set-membership
# check on the algebra's element-set).
bilateral translation_witnessing {
  sentinel "translation=discharged"
  arity    1
}
translation_witnessing(outcome: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === translate_rust_to_mirror — the composition action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING COMPOSITION ACTION. Given a source ref (a `.rs`
# path at `@code/rust` altitude) + a target shard-path ref (a
# `.mirror` path at `@mirror` altitude), composes the 9-edge
# autopoietic Rust→mirror translation per the docblock composition
# graph above. Returns `@glass.verdict`.
#
# The action body is `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-
# not-deliver]]. Reed follow-up ticks realise the composition edges
# through `apply_h::act` dispatch:
#
#   Follow-up A (this species; discharged THIS tick): substrate-decl
#     the composition edge as first-class named action.
#
#   Follow-up B (Reed): seed `@silicon/algebra` with the 21 mirror-
#     authored bilateral retirements as crystals via Bridge γ
#     existing surface. Extends the empirical memory to the 21-arm
#     surface without running the Rust→mirror translation loop from
#     scratch. Per canonical spec §6.2.
#
#   Follow-up C (Reed): realise `@fate.roll` + `@glue.compose`
#     resolvers so the composition becomes invocable via
#     `apply_h::act`. The `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` bypass
#     applies IFF the resolver requires primitive @io semantics no
#     shard body can provide (per feedback-no-rust-extension-
#     shortcut); otherwise the resolver composes as a shard body over
#     @io.
#
#   Follow-up D (empirical run): `mirror roomba --translate=<rs-file>`
#     invokes THIS action; the compiler authors the deletion +
#     translation commits per bilateral_arm_redundant precedent
#     (`ad52973` + `20047c2` shape at translation altitude); every
#     discharge grows `@kintsugi/algebra` by one turn.
#
# The `requires translation_witnessing(outcome)` clause names the
# discharge condition per recognition #37 (Pask-agreement reading
# of `requires`): the action's body commits to producing an outcome
# for which `translation_witnessing(outcome) = Pass`; consumers
# surface violations at the species boundary.
#
# Identity contract for the action's outcome: byte-equality on
# (source.oid, target_shard_path.oid, winning_fracture.oid,
# selected_morphism.oid, payload.oid). Two invocations with byte-
# equal source + target that select the same winning fracture and
# same morphism produce byte-equal outcomes under content-addressing.
translate_rust_to_mirror(
  source:            ref,
  target_shard_path: ref,
) -> verdict
requires translation_witnessing(outcome)
{ \ }

out @kintsugi/translate
out translation_witnessing
out translate_rust_to_mirror
